<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §4 — the coolant eel.

    Odyssey-only by construction: ParentName="FishBase" is an Odyssey abstract,
    and the whole fishing stack (WaterBodyTracker, Zone_Fishing, JobDriver_Fish,
    NegativeFishingOutcomeDef) ships with Odyssey. MayRequire keeps the def out
    of the load entirely on an Odyssey-less install rather than erroring on a
    missing parent.

    Register law (sheet §6): §P only. Ban 1 — nothing here may say the catch is
    noticed, priced, or watched; the description is what a Jawa with the fish in
    hand can see, and stops there. Ban 2 — no explanation of why it lives where
    it lives. The eel being SALABLE is the sheet's own line ("eel-catch —
    salable, watched"); the "watched" half is mechanism and stays out of text.

    MarketValue 18 is the kit spec's own INVENTED figure for §4 ("eel market
    value ~18"). FishBase's own 6.5 is the plain-food baseline; piranha at 40 is
    the trophy end. 18 reads as "worth the trip, not a fortune".

    Placeholder art: texPath points at vanilla's dogfish sprite, the same
    "reuse a vanilla asset until the art pipe runs" convention §1/§2/§3 used.
    A real eel sprite is a one-line swap.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="FishBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_CoolantEel</defName>
    <label>coolant eel</label>
    <description>A pale, eyeless eel as long as a forearm, cold to the touch long after it leaves the water. Its skin is smooth and faintly metallic, and it goes on twitching for a while after it stops living. Buyers off-plateau pay well for one.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Fish/Dogfish</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>18</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
